{"name":"Velvet Rope","hex":"#36526a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"velvet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A closely woven fabric (originally of silk, now also of cotton or man-made fibres) with a thick short pile on one side.","Very fine fur, including the skin and fur on a deer's antlers."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover with velvet or with a covering of a similar texture.","To coat raw meat in starch, then in oil, preparatory to frying."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/velvet"},{"term":"rope","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Thick strings, yarn, monofilaments, metal wires, or strands of other cordage that are twisted together to form a stronger line.","An individual length of such material."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To tie (something) with rope.","To throw a rope (or something similar, e.g. a lasso, cable, wire, etc.) around (something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rope"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Velvet Rope","blocks":[{"text":"The Velvet Rope is the sixth studio album by American singer Janet Jackson. It was released on October 7, 1997, through Virgin Records. Prior to its release, Jackson renegotiated her contract with Virgin for US$80 million, marking this as the largest recording contract in history at that time."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6b/Janet_Jackson_%E2%80%93_The_Velvet_Rope_%28Official_Album_Cover%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Velvet_Rope","wikidata":"Q777308"},{"title":"Velvet","blocks":[{"text":"Velvet is a type of woven fabric with a dense, even pile that gives it a distinctive soft feel. Historically, velvet was typically made from silk. Modern velvet can be made from silk, linen, cotton, wool, synthetic fibers, silk-cotton blends, or synthetic-natural fiber blends."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Blue_velvet_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Velvet","wikidata":"Q243519"},{"title":"Rope","blocks":[{"text":"A rope is a group of yarns, plies, fibres, or strands that are twisted or braided together into a larger and stronger form. Ropes have high tensile strength and can be used for dragging and lifting. Rope is thicker and stronger than similarly constructed cord, string, and twine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/Cordage_en_chanvre.jpg/330px-Cordage_en_chanvre.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rope","wikidata":"Q31029"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/EllenVonUnwerth_-_FilipNaudts.jpg/500px-EllenVonUnwerth_-_FilipNaudts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/EllenVonUnwerth_-_FilipNaudts.jpg/1280px-EllenVonUnwerth_-_FilipNaudts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/EllenVonUnwerth_-_FilipNaudts.jpg/500px-EllenVonUnwerth_-_FilipNaudts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photographer Ellen von Unwerth (pictured) attempted to capture Jackson's emotional pain within the album's imagery.[17]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEllenVonUnwerth_-_FilipNaudts.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Janet_Jackson_Velvet_Rope_Tour_live_in_Milano_1998.jpg/500px-Janet_Jackson_Velvet_Rope_Tour_live_in_Milano_1998.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Janet_Jackson_Velvet_Rope_Tour_live_in_M